chul", "Consistent polling lead of 8-16 points across pollsters, including Republican-sponsored surveys", "Prediction markets price Hochul at 94-96% to win", "Blakeman's fundraising ($13.4M) is competitive but hasn't closed the gap"], "rationale": "Every poll since March shows Hochul ahead by at least 4 points, with most showing double digits, and even Republican-leaning pollsters find her leading. All six expert ratings place the race in the Safe or Solid D column, and markets price a Hochul win above 94%, so a modest trim from the fundamentals-based margin to match the polling average is warranted.", "watch": "Utility costs and energy affordability have become the central debate theme; a strong Blakeman debate performance or a polling shift toward the low single digits would move this toward Likely D.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Kathy Hochul (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Incumbent Governor Kathy Hochul seeks a second full term against Nassau County Executive Bruce Blakeman in a state that leans Democratic by eight points. Polling throughout 2026 has consistently shown Hochul ahead, with recent surveys from August showing margins of 4 to 16 points, including leads in polls sponsored by Republican-leaning firms. Blakeman has raised a competitive $13.4 million, but Hochul's cash position and incumbency remain advantages.\n\nThe closing debate has centered on utility bills and Hochul's energy rebate program, with Republicans attempting to nationalize the race around affordability. All major raters call the race Safe or Solid Democratic, and prediction markets price Hochul's chances above 94 percent. The race appears settled barring a major late shift.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9859, "margin": 12.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.97, "margin": 11.0}]}